[[2115,803,"Evidence was given by prison staff that it was not uncommon for prisoners to be under the influence of substances, particularly spice at HMP Rochester","prisoners under influence of substances",""],[2116,803,"Prison staff did not receive a briefing about prisoners with medication in possession in accordance with PS24/2011","lack of medication possession briefing",""],[2117,803,"In evidence there were discrepancies between the policies in place and the understanding of healthcare staff as to what information could be shared with prison staff and when it should be shared","information sharing policy discrepancy",""],[3955,1488,"evidence was given at the inquest that some officers chairing reviews did not read relevant documentation beyond the last ACCT review prior to the review taking place","incomplete risk assessment",""],[3956,1488,"Some of the officers chairing reviews did not understand how to complete the support plan paperwork such that the ACCT was closed when some of the support plans had not started or had not been completed","premature closure of ACCT",""]]